3321.85},"playbook":{"commit":"7b4e5ddcb84caa772e584b8ddfb637f6168f800a","files":{"b0-monthly-sc-v1.yaml":"# B0: a MEASUREMENT shadow (story R3, owner decision 1 A, 16 Oct 2026). Never promoted: approving it to paper needs the\n# owner's own decision, which this label does not grant. Experiment 1's policy P1 exactly (response 92's B0 row). P1\n# lost Rs 34,486 over 60 opportunities in 2019-23 (Rs 23,140 without 7 impossible stale-close exits;\n# research/2026-10-12-experiment-1/RESULTS.md). It measures premium, costs and the fill path at real quotes and can\n# never show an edge. Idea card: research/ideas/B0.md.\nname: b0-monthly-sc\nversion: 1\nstatus: research\npayer: >-\n  Measurement only, no claimed payer: option buyers may overpay for NIFTY index protection (variance risk premium,\n  implied above realised by a median 2 points), but experiment 1 found no edge after costs. B0 records the real\n  premium, costs and fills at 15:00 quotes.\nedge_family: measurement\nstructure:\n  code: SC\n  strikes_rule: sell the call nearest spot x 1.02 and the put nearest spot x 0.98 (entry day's chain), buy each W further out\n  width_rule: largest W of 300, 250, 200, 150, 100 points whose modelled maximum loss incl. charges and pads is at most Rs 10,000\n  widths: [300, 250, 200, 150, 100]\n  lots: 1\n  expiry:\n    kind: monthly\n    min_days: 30\n    max_days: 45\n    exit_days_before_expiry: 21\nentry_conditions: []\nlive_use_rule:\n  min_days: 20\n  min_agreement: 0.9\n  min_available: 0.9\nsize_rule: 1 lot (65 units); no trade if the modelled maximum loss incl. charges exceeds Rs 10,000\nfunding:\n  margin_per_lot: 67595\n  # NSE's initial margin, not C2's stressed margin (about 98,013 at k 1.45) or the funds at entry (about Rs 1,00,784)\n  source: NSE SPAN plus exposure for SC 300, 14 Oct 2026 (research/data/margins/margins.csv; response 92)\n  date: 2026-10-14\nexits:\n  time: the last trading day with 21 or more calendar days to expiry, at 15:00\n  profit: none  # held to the time exit\n  loss: none  # nothing beyond the bought wings: the maximum loss is capped at entry\n  event: none\nevaluation_plan:\n  expected_range:  # P1's 10th-90th percentile single-trade net, 58 traded cycles 2019-23 (results_challenge.json);\n  # a range of single trades, while E6's review compares the mean with its low: restate it before B0 reaches 20 positions\n    low: -5084\n    high: 4156\n  expected_net_per_opportunity: -386\n  expected_net_source: experiment 1 challenge 2019-2023, P1, -Rs 23,140 over 60 opportunities without 7 impossible stale-close exits (-Rs 34,486 with them); worst clean trade -8,937\n  unit: Rs C1 net per opportunity after charges and pads, before tax\n  review_dates:\n    - 2027-01-15\n    - 2027-04-15\n  pause_rules:\n    - a single trade loses Rs 10,000 or more including charges (E6 alerts; a research version is never paused, the owner decides)\n    - realised net at or below -Rs 30,000 (3 x cap; E6 alerts; expected for a measurement, not a defect)\n  catastrophic_loss_rs: 10000\nevidence:\n  test_results_path: null\n  test_results_commit: null\n  red_team_note: null\n  judge_verdict: null\n  freeze_record: null\n  owner_approval_date: null\n","example-sc-iv-rich-no-event-v1.yaml":"# WORKED EXAMPLE of the playbook format (story D1). NOT A PASSED STRATEGY and never to be approved as it stands.\n# Its rule is experiment 1's policy P6 (\"SC if F1 > 0 and no event\"), which FAILED the 2019-2023 challenge:\n# -Rs 18,468 over 60 opportunities (research/2026-10-12-experiment-1/RESULTS.md). The funding and expected-range\n# numbers below are illustrative, not measured. Status stays `research`; the evidence stays empty.\nname: example-sc-iv-rich-no-event\nversion: 1\nstatus: research\npayer: >-\n  Hypothesis only: option buyers who overpay for NIFTY index protection when implied volatility is above realised\n  volatility (the variance risk premium). Experiment 1 found no such edge after costs in 2019-2023.\nedge_family: short premium, defined risk\nstructure:\n  code: SC\n  strikes_rule: sell the call nearest spot x 1.02 and the put nearest spot x 0.98 (entry day's chain), buy each W further out\n  width_rule: largest W of 300, 250, 200, 150, 100 points whose modelled maximum loss incl. charges and pads is at most Rs 10,000\n  widths: [300, 250, 200, 150, 100]\n  lots: 1\n  expiry:\n    kind: monthly\n    min_days: 30\n    max_days: 45\n    exit_days_before_expiry: 21\nentry_conditions:\n  - feature: F1_atm_iv_minus_rv20\n    operator: \">\"\n    threshold: 0\n  - feature: F3_scheduled_event_in_window\n    operator: is\n    threshold: false\nlive_use_rule:\n  min_days: 20\n  min_agreement: 0.9\n  min_available: 0.9\nsize_rule: 1 lot (65 units); no trade if the modelled maximum loss incl. charges exceeds Rs 10,000\nfunding:\n  margin_per_lot: 20000\n  source: ILLUSTRATIVE, not measured (research/data/margins/margins.csv has no SC row yet)\n  date: 2026-10-14\nexits:\n  time: the last trading day with 21 or more calendar days to expiry, at 15:00\n  profit: none  # held to the time exit\n  loss: none  # nothing beyond the bought wings: the maximum loss is capped at entry\n  event: none\nevaluation_plan:\n  expected_range:\n    low: -1500\n    high: 500\n  expected_net_per_opportunity: -308\n  expected_net_source: experiment 1 challenge 2019-2023, P6, -Rs 18,468 over 60 opportunities (a FAIL)\n  unit: Rs net per opportunity after charges, pads and 31.2% tax (illustrative)\n  review_dates:\n    - 2027-01-14\n    - 2027-04-14\n  pause_rules:\n    - a single trade loses more than Rs 10,000 including charges (catastrophic-loss rule)\n    - the book's drawdown brake (Rs 30,000 below its highest closed equity)\n  catastrophic_loss_rs: 10000\nevidence:\n  test_results_path: null\n  test_results_commit: null\n  red_team_note: null\n  judge_verdict: null\n  freeze_record: null\n  owner_approval_date: null\n"},"registry_csv":"name,version,sha256,status,changed_on,approved_by,evidence_commit\nb0-monthly-sc,